From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 10:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211_hwsim: make the interface limit of a radio a parameter

A radio combines up to 2048 interfaces of the station, AP, mesh and P2P
types, far more than hardware does. Userspace that derives the number of
BSSes a radio supports from the interface combinations then reports a
value no real radio has.

Add the max_interfaces module parameter for that limit. It keeps 2048 by
default.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
@@ -72,6 +72,11 @@ static bool mlo;
 module_param(mlo, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(mlo, "Support MLO");
 
+static u16 max_interfaces = 2048;
+module_param(max_interfaces, ushort, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(max_interfaces,
+		 "Interfaces of the station, AP, mesh and P2P types a radio combines");
+
 static bool multi_radio;
 module_param(multi_radio, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(multi_radio, "Support Multiple Radios per wiphy");
@@ -5926,7 +5931,7 @@ static int mac80211_hwsim_new_radio(stru
 	}
 
 	if (param->iftypes & HWSIM_DEFAULT_IF_LIMIT) {
-		data->if_limits[n_limits].max = 2048;
+		data->if_limits[n_limits].max = max_interfaces ?: 1;
 		/*
 		 * For this case, we may only support a subset of
 		 * HWSIM_DEFAULT_IF_LIMIT, therefore we only want to add the
